WEBVTT

00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:06.840
Ten. Nine. Eight.

00:00:07.250 --> 00:00:08.800
Seven. Six.

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:10.760
Five. Four.

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:11.720
Three.

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:13.550
Two. One.

00:00:13.630 --> 00:00:14.510
Zero!

00:00:31.070 --> 00:00:33.150
<i>For providing us with electricity,</i>

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:36.280
<i>let's give the Shibuya Defense Service</i>
<i>a round of applause!</i>

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:41.450
We only lent them
the String Puppet's power source unit.

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:44.210
Now, now. Let's just be grateful
for future technology.

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:48.420
<i>Who would have guessed it would be enough</i>
<i>to supply all of Shibuya's power?</i>

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:52.340
Gai!

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:53.760
Marin!

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:54.760
Keisaku!

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:55.880
Lu!

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:58.350
<i>What the hell?</i>

00:00:58.550 --> 00:01:00.430
<i>Don't I have any fans?</i>

00:01:00.510 --> 00:01:02.310
<i>There should at least be one.</i>

00:01:02.470 --> 00:01:04.890
<i>Don't you know I'm the team leader?</i>

00:02:43.030 --> 00:02:43.870
You hit it.

00:02:43.950 --> 00:02:46.200
-Yes!
-The Civilian?

00:02:46.290 --> 00:02:48.660
It's withdrawing. It was a success.

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:50.460
The training paid off.

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:53.750
Good job. Now you're an asset
to the force, Marimari.

00:02:54.130 --> 00:02:55.630
I'm so glad!

00:02:55.710 --> 00:02:58.970
I've been training nonstop
these past three weeks.

00:02:59.050 --> 00:03:01.680
Then you two deserve a gift.

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:05.260
Only the guys need
to go on patrol tomorrow.

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:07.270
The girls can have the day off.

00:03:07.350 --> 00:03:09.350
-Yes!
-Yes!

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:15.440
I'm sorry. If we let you have autographs,
we have to give them to everyone.

00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:17.980
We can't give you special treatment.

00:03:21.410 --> 00:03:23.370
I don't mind giving an autograph.

00:03:24.570 --> 00:03:26.280
Thank you, mister!

00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:29.710
You're welcome. It's no big deal.

00:03:29.790 --> 00:03:32.330
What the heck is Daisuke doing?

00:03:32.420 --> 00:03:33.500
Leave him alone.

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:35.840
Let him enjoy his hero moment.

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:36.920
It's not good.

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:38.840
Even though the electricity is back,

00:03:38.920 --> 00:03:40.920
we've been living like this
for a month now.

00:03:41.010 --> 00:03:44.850
But still, thanks to the electricity,
they've been able to search underground.

00:03:44.930 --> 00:03:47.850
I hear they found an abundant supply
of canned food and drinking water.

00:03:47.970 --> 00:03:49.890
There's a water
recirculating system now too.

00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:53.730
-The situation is slowly getting better.
-I'm talking about our mental readiness.

00:03:53.850 --> 00:03:56.730
You know, you'll burn yourself out
if you're always on edge.

00:03:56.820 --> 00:03:57.730
Yes.

00:03:58.280 --> 00:03:59.150
Still...

00:03:59.860 --> 00:04:01.280
Oh man!

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:04.110
She asked me for everyone's autographs--

00:04:05.410 --> 00:04:06.660
But seriously,

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:10.330
is it really okay for them
to provide so much space just for us?

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:11.790
It's to be expected.

00:04:11.910 --> 00:04:15.210
We need everything prepared
so we can respond if something happens.

00:04:15.330 --> 00:04:17.630
It's like a real secret hideout!

00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:20.800
-Yes.
-Don't be ridiculous. This isn't a game.

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:22.800
-We know that.
-No, you don't.

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:25.680
What about the people
who have been captured?

00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:28.310
You know what, Gai?

00:04:29.430 --> 00:04:30.810
Daisuke's uncle

00:04:31.310 --> 00:04:33.940
and my mom are still being held hostage.

00:04:34.810 --> 00:04:37.230
Of course we're not going
to give up on them.

00:04:38.020 --> 00:04:39.780
You're right. I went too far.

00:04:40.360 --> 00:04:43.740
But we'd go crazy
if we kept it all inside.

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:45.990
Let us have a breather now and then.

00:04:47.370 --> 00:04:48.700
Sorry, Daisuke.

00:04:48.780 --> 00:04:50.910
It's okay, but you have to sign this.

00:04:51.910 --> 00:04:53.460
Jeez, man.

00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:56.370
All right. Where's the pen?

00:04:56.460 --> 00:04:59.040
I think there was one in the girls' room.

00:05:01.130 --> 00:05:03.510
How do you know that? Did you go in...

00:05:03.590 --> 00:05:04.760
GIRLS

00:05:04.840 --> 00:05:06.590
-I'm just joking--
-Keisaku.

00:05:06.680 --> 00:05:08.760
Why are you going in there
without permission?

00:05:08.850 --> 00:05:10.720
What bad timing.

00:05:11.390 --> 00:05:13.060
Could it be that you're...

00:05:13.180 --> 00:05:15.390
The reason our panties went missing?

00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:16.560
-What?
-That happened?

00:05:16.650 --> 00:05:18.270
He can go to prison for now.

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:20.190
No, to the gallows.

00:05:20.730 --> 00:05:21.820
It wasn't me!

00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:22.940
I didn't do it!

00:05:23.030 --> 00:05:25.110
That's a pretty bad joke to play.

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:27.570
Please, you got to believe me!

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:34.290
-Should we let him off the hook?
-Yes.

00:05:34.370 --> 00:05:37.420
I'll be more considerate next time.
I'm sorry.

00:05:38.420 --> 00:05:41.380
-What about the panties incident?
-We were just kidding.

00:05:43.210 --> 00:05:44.590
THANK YOU FOR THE PEACE

00:05:44.670 --> 00:05:45.510
SHIBUYA LOVE

00:05:47.090 --> 00:05:49.300
Good luck, Marimari!

00:05:49.390 --> 00:05:50.220
KEISAKU

00:05:50.300 --> 00:05:51.220
V FOR VICTORY

00:05:51.810 --> 00:05:54.140
<i>The group formed to save Shibuya!</i>

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:57.520
<i>The heroes of justice!</i>
<i>The Superhero Puppet Squad SDS!</i>

00:05:58.650 --> 00:06:00.900
You two stop horsing around and focus!

00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:04.900
<i>We're in the middle of a patrol.</i>
<i>You need to keep an eye out.</i>

00:06:04.990 --> 00:06:05.990
<i>-Roger!</i>
<i>-Got it!</i>

00:06:06.070 --> 00:06:10.570
<i>-Keisaku, you should say "Roger" too.</i>
<i>-Why does it matter how you say it?</i>

00:06:10.660 --> 00:06:13.830
<i>-I'm the leader. That's an order!</i>
<i>-Why, you little--</i>

00:06:13.910 --> 00:06:17.710
<i>Heroes should have exemplary conduct.</i>
<i>The SDS should act like proper gentlemen!</i>

00:06:19.420 --> 00:06:21.630
High school kids have so much energy.

00:06:23.500 --> 00:06:28.300
No, it's okay. I'm still in my twenties.
Don't sell yourself short, Officer Izumi!

00:06:29.050 --> 00:06:32.100
Yes, we still have access
to many educational institutions,

00:06:32.180 --> 00:06:33.720
so we can prevent the spread of disease.

00:06:33.810 --> 00:06:37.020
I see. Then the next issue
is agricultural produce.

00:06:37.140 --> 00:06:39.940
Can we do something
around the Broadcasting Center?

00:06:40.020 --> 00:06:42.650
We need to plan early for food provision.

00:06:42.730 --> 00:06:45.360
What if we ask AHRV for support?

00:06:49.110 --> 00:06:52.030
We really are in the future, huh?

00:06:52.740 --> 00:06:55.990
It's hard to believe
this is the middle of Tokyo.

00:06:56.750 --> 00:06:58.250
You look happy, Daisuke.

00:06:58.500 --> 00:07:00.000
What? I do?

00:07:00.250 --> 00:07:04.500
Well, I don't mind that the five of us
are back to how we used to be.

00:07:04.750 --> 00:07:05.590
Right.

00:07:06.250 --> 00:07:09.220
And now, people wave to us on the streets.

00:07:09.930 --> 00:07:12.430
It makes me feel like I'm protecting them.

00:07:13.350 --> 00:07:14.970
That makes me feel happy.

00:07:17.560 --> 00:07:22.150
You never stopped saying that you want
to protect people since that incident.

00:07:22.230 --> 00:07:25.690
I thought maybe you'd gone crazy.
Now it's become reality.

00:07:25.770 --> 00:07:27.400
Do you remember what happened back then?

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:30.700
Yes, we were all going to go
to the summer festival together,

00:07:30.780 --> 00:07:32.610
but you played a trick on me.

00:07:32.700 --> 00:07:35.870
Sorry about that.
It was just supposed to be a prank.

00:07:36.200 --> 00:07:39.160
But then you ended up disappearing.

00:07:41.870 --> 00:07:43.540
Why isn't Daisuke here?

00:07:43.880 --> 00:07:44.960
What should we do?

00:07:45.170 --> 00:07:47.380
Should we go to the festival
without Daisuke?

00:07:47.460 --> 00:07:49.920
He always has the worst luck.

00:07:50.590 --> 00:07:52.590
I wonder what happened to Daisuke?

00:07:53.130 --> 00:07:57.560
<i>I didn't have the courage to ask Marimari</i>
<i>to go to the festival alone with me.</i>

00:07:58.640 --> 00:08:01.270
<i>So I wanted to distance you from her.</i>

00:08:02.190 --> 00:08:03.270
<i>I'm the worst.</i>

00:08:04.020 --> 00:08:05.650
<i>Where's your status report?</i>

00:08:05.730 --> 00:08:08.230
Don't be such a hard-ass.
We were just reminiscing.

00:08:08.320 --> 00:08:10.860
You can chat
after you've finished your job.

00:08:10.940 --> 00:08:11.950
<i>Okay.</i>

00:08:12.030 --> 00:08:13.070
Status?

00:08:13.410 --> 00:08:14.410
<i>All clear.</i>

00:08:14.490 --> 00:08:17.120
Understood. All clear here, as well.

00:08:17.240 --> 00:08:19.240
<i>Oh, Milo. That's where you are.</i>

00:08:19.410 --> 00:08:21.960
<i>Damn. I should have gone with that unit.</i>

00:08:22.960 --> 00:08:26.040
What is that supposed to mean?
Do you want to switch assignments?

00:08:26.130 --> 00:08:27.790
He wants to be with you.

00:08:28.590 --> 00:08:32.170
When we return, he can see me anytime.
Besides, we're in the middle of a mission.

00:08:32.920 --> 00:08:35.550
You're right, but...

00:08:35.970 --> 00:08:38.390
<i>Maybe I'll give him a stronger warning.</i>

00:08:38.810 --> 00:08:41.180
Daisuke! I'll tell you this now.

00:08:41.640 --> 00:08:44.190
<i>Don't get us mixed up</i>
<i>in your past hang-ups.</i>

00:08:44.480 --> 00:08:45.690
<i>Focus on reality!</i>

00:08:45.980 --> 00:08:48.480
<i>You're a second-year high school student.</i>
<i>You're too old for this!</i>

00:08:48.570 --> 00:08:49.690
That's going too far, moron.

00:08:49.770 --> 00:08:53.190
But Milo showed up, right?
Everything was true.

00:08:53.280 --> 00:08:55.410
You're the one who needs to face reality!

00:08:55.490 --> 00:08:58.030
<i>You're the one who's going nuts</i>
<i>in this future society.</i>

00:08:58.120 --> 00:08:59.200
What did you say?

00:08:59.410 --> 00:09:01.410
Why, you lazy-ass NEET!

00:09:01.490 --> 00:09:02.790
That does it!

00:09:02.870 --> 00:09:04.330
Stop! That's dangerous!

00:09:04.410 --> 00:09:05.620
<i>What are you doing?</i>

00:09:05.710 --> 00:09:07.540
What? Well, you know...

00:09:08.290 --> 00:09:11.920
It's certain
that the future Milo saves us, right?

00:09:12.090 --> 00:09:13.630
Predictions of the future...

00:09:13.720 --> 00:09:15.840
That's what it means, right Milo?

00:09:16.430 --> 00:09:17.550
For now, at least.

00:09:17.640 --> 00:09:20.810
What? Don't say it like that.

00:09:21.260 --> 00:09:24.180
In any case, keep a good lookout.

00:09:24.430 --> 00:09:29.270
We're not just looking for Civilians.
We need clues to find the Revisions' base.

00:09:29.360 --> 00:09:31.230
I know that already!

00:09:34.110 --> 00:09:37.030
Release me already.

00:09:37.110 --> 00:09:41.490
If we don't reopen negotiations
with the Revisions, we'll lose our gains.

00:09:41.580 --> 00:09:46.000
Are you aware that we're no longer
running electricity from our generators?

00:09:46.410 --> 00:09:50.170
It's being supplied by the power units
from the String Puppets.

00:09:50.540 --> 00:09:53.050
We've discovered sources
of gas and water too.

00:09:53.170 --> 00:09:57.680
The food you've also been eating,
was transported from underground.

00:09:58.260 --> 00:10:01.600
The train station building is now prepared
for hydroponic farming.

00:10:01.680 --> 00:10:04.930
There's no way that will be enough
to feed everyone!

00:10:05.020 --> 00:10:06.680
How many people do you think there are?

00:10:06.770 --> 00:10:07.940
-Exactly.
-What?

00:10:08.020 --> 00:10:10.560
We'd like to solve
the food issue at least.

00:10:10.730 --> 00:10:11.770
You...

00:10:14.690 --> 00:10:16.150
What is it, Gai?

00:10:17.070 --> 00:10:19.910
I'm sorry.
I'll come back if this is a bad time.

00:10:19.990 --> 00:10:20.990
No, it's fine.

00:10:22.490 --> 00:10:23.490
Mr. Muta,

00:10:23.700 --> 00:10:26.910
are you saying that the Revisions
would be able to provide food?

00:10:27.330 --> 00:10:29.370
How about AHRV?

00:10:29.460 --> 00:10:30.670
How would I know?

00:10:30.750 --> 00:10:32.590
We didn't talk about that!

00:10:33.500 --> 00:10:37.220
I'm going to return every single person
in Shibuya back to 2017.

00:10:37.380 --> 00:10:38.550
That's a promise.

00:10:39.130 --> 00:10:40.590
I wanted the same...

00:10:40.680 --> 00:10:42.180
Gai, let's talk upstairs.

00:10:42.600 --> 00:10:45.010
Mr. Muta, you'll stay here for now.

00:10:45.560 --> 00:10:49.230
We'll let you out only if we need you
to talk to the Revisions.

00:10:49.810 --> 00:10:50.730
Wait!

00:10:50.810 --> 00:10:51.900
Wait!

00:10:52.020 --> 00:10:54.190
This is a violation of human rights!

00:10:54.270 --> 00:10:56.730
There are no human rights
in Shibuya right now.

00:10:56.860 --> 00:10:57.860
Especially not for you!

00:10:57.940 --> 00:10:59.700
<i>That man...</i>

00:11:00.160 --> 00:11:03.320
<i>He doesn't plan on letting me</i>
<i>return to the present!</i>

00:11:11.960 --> 00:11:13.920
<i>This feels so good!</i>

00:11:17.050 --> 00:11:20.260
Is it really okay for us
to have this all to ourselves?

00:11:20.470 --> 00:11:21.470
It's fine.

00:11:21.550 --> 00:11:24.390
This is part of the arrangements
for the SDS.

00:11:26.390 --> 00:11:29.600
It's apparently like a special allowance
for hazardous work.

00:11:30.350 --> 00:11:32.350
Like a way of paying us in kind?

00:11:32.480 --> 00:11:34.060
Those are pretty big.

00:11:34.690 --> 00:11:36.400
You've got nice boobs.

00:11:36.520 --> 00:11:37.780
Do I?

00:11:38.440 --> 00:11:41.070
No wonder you had so many fans in school.

00:11:41.150 --> 00:11:43.070
Oh, you! Stop that.

00:11:43.160 --> 00:11:45.410
Now, now. No need to hide them.

00:11:45.490 --> 00:11:47.540
Cut it out!

00:11:48.910 --> 00:11:51.370
I see. A search party, huh?

00:11:51.460 --> 00:11:54.880
Yes. Both Daisuke and Keisaku's family
are hostages,

00:11:55.040 --> 00:11:57.460
so I'm sure it's harder for them to ask.

00:11:57.550 --> 00:11:59.260
However...

00:11:59.630 --> 00:12:00.920
Is there a problem?

00:12:01.010 --> 00:12:03.680
In order to spare some of our forces
for a search party,

00:12:03.760 --> 00:12:06.930
the SDS needs to be a solid team.

00:12:07.720 --> 00:12:09.640
But Daisuke Dojima...

00:12:10.680 --> 00:12:11.680
I get what you mean.

00:12:12.520 --> 00:12:16.150
Gai, Officer Izumi is part of SDS,

00:12:16.440 --> 00:12:18.690
but Daisuke is not cut out
to be a team leader.

00:12:18.780 --> 00:12:21.610
Milo is an outsider.
She's more like a mentor.

00:12:23.700 --> 00:12:24.820
You are the leader.

00:12:25.530 --> 00:12:27.950
You won't officially be appointed
until later,

00:12:28.080 --> 00:12:29.490
but keep that in mind.

00:12:29.700 --> 00:12:30.830
When that happens,

00:12:30.910 --> 00:12:34.460
I can send a search party
to look for the Revision's hideout.

00:12:34.580 --> 00:12:35.420
Understood.

00:12:35.750 --> 00:12:39.170
We will have our regular meeting later,
I'd like you to join us.

00:12:39.250 --> 00:12:42.630
It's important to have
the people involved know your face.

00:12:43.170 --> 00:12:44.300
Yes, sir.

00:12:46.260 --> 00:12:47.220
Where's Milo?

00:12:47.300 --> 00:12:49.600
I invited her but she turned me down.

00:12:50.600 --> 00:12:53.890
Milo looks about the same age as you guys,
but I wonder how old she is.

00:12:53.980 --> 00:12:57.610
That's true, we've never asked her.
Right, Marimari?

00:12:58.400 --> 00:12:59.360
Yes.

00:13:00.400 --> 00:13:02.650
Why are you spacing out?
Is it too hot for you?

00:13:03.320 --> 00:13:05.860
I just remembered that today...

00:13:06.490 --> 00:13:09.280
-Today?
-Today is Daisuke's birthday, isn't it?

00:13:10.620 --> 00:13:13.120
Now that you mention it, you may be right.

00:13:13.290 --> 00:13:16.920
Maybe we can do something to celebrate.
Like a cake, maybe?

00:13:17.040 --> 00:13:18.130
A cake?

00:13:18.210 --> 00:13:19.630
Getting a strawberry shortcake

00:13:19.710 --> 00:13:21.960
or roll cake is impossible
in this situation.

00:13:23.670 --> 00:13:25.880
Wait. We might have the ingredients.

00:13:25.970 --> 00:13:30.180
Marimari, you used to like Daisuke
in the past, didn't you?

00:13:30.260 --> 00:13:33.270
-What?
-No use hiding it. It's so obvious!

00:13:33.350 --> 00:13:35.980
You seemed to be
keeping your distance lately, but...

00:13:36.060 --> 00:13:40.480
What? Did seeing him in action
make him seem cool?

00:13:41.150 --> 00:13:43.360
Well, how should I put it...

00:13:43.780 --> 00:13:46.610
He seems more relaxed since coming here.

00:13:46.700 --> 00:13:50.330
He's able to talk with everyone
more normally.

00:13:50.410 --> 00:13:54.080
So, you know...

00:13:54.160 --> 00:13:55.540
-Well...
-I've got it!

00:13:55.870 --> 00:13:57.500
I'll take care of the cake.

00:13:57.580 --> 00:13:59.040
Leave it to me!

00:14:02.380 --> 00:14:03.960
<i>As I've told you already,</i>

00:14:04.050 --> 00:14:08.430
the amount of electricity the power unit,
the Cube, can supply is limited.

00:14:08.510 --> 00:14:12.850
It was originally created as the battery
for powering the String Puppets.

00:14:12.930 --> 00:14:15.560
You said it has about a month's worth
of power left.

00:14:15.640 --> 00:14:17.810
It depends on what the Revisions do.

00:14:19.230 --> 00:14:22.820
Therefore, we'd like to limit
the use of power going forward.

00:14:22.900 --> 00:14:25.400
The list of facilities is in front of you.

00:14:25.490 --> 00:14:29.990
Having a power supply
for the medical facilities is a godsend.

00:14:30.070 --> 00:14:31.700
We have to hand it to AHRV.

00:14:32.530 --> 00:14:33.910
You're right.

00:14:34.490 --> 00:14:36.250
I apologize for my tardiness.

00:14:38.870 --> 00:14:42.960
As I've often told you,
the Revisions will no doubt attack again.

00:14:43.750 --> 00:14:45.760
Just as with colleagues in AHRV,

00:14:45.840 --> 00:14:47.420
the people of Shibuya

00:14:47.670 --> 00:14:50.430
must be necessary
for their human experiment.

00:14:51.680 --> 00:14:55.560
Until reinforcements from AHRV arrive,
we must find a way to survive on our own.

00:14:55.640 --> 00:14:57.980
Ms. Milo, when will AHRV be arriving?

00:14:58.730 --> 00:15:02.650
We'd like to also ask for help
in providing food and clothing.

00:15:02.730 --> 00:15:05.650
I have not heard anything regarding that.

00:15:05.900 --> 00:15:08.360
But when the time comes,
I will let you know, of course.

00:15:09.280 --> 00:15:10.320
I see.

00:15:11.490 --> 00:15:14.700
-Any other topics of discussion?
-Yes! This is regarding SDS.

00:15:14.780 --> 00:15:18.700
-What is it?
-Today is Daisuke Dojima's birthday.

00:15:18.910 --> 00:15:23.790
Ms. Temari suggested we have
a celebration with a cake.

00:15:23.880 --> 00:15:25.590
-What?
-What?

00:15:27.670 --> 00:15:28.550
Oh, no.

00:15:28.630 --> 00:15:30.760
Does that need to be discussed here?

00:15:30.840 --> 00:15:31.840
Understood.

00:15:32.220 --> 00:15:35.890
I'm certain these times have been tough
for Gai and the others.

00:15:36.720 --> 00:15:39.270
It may help improve their motivation.

00:15:39.980 --> 00:15:41.890
I'll talk to the staff
and prepare something.

00:15:41.980 --> 00:15:43.440
Thank you!

00:15:49.530 --> 00:15:51.700
<i>Formation Pattern A.</i>

00:15:52.990 --> 00:15:54.120
<i>Listen, Izumi.</i>

00:15:54.320 --> 00:15:55.620
<i>In preparation for later,</i>

00:15:55.700 --> 00:15:58.080
I want you to take field command
this time.

00:15:58.160 --> 00:16:00.000
<i>Roger. Leave it to me.</i>

00:16:00.620 --> 00:16:02.790
<i>You may not get a turn today, Gai.</i>
<i>It'll be easy--</i>

00:16:02.870 --> 00:16:04.670
<i>Keisaku, you've got one behind you!</i>

00:16:05.330 --> 00:16:07.750
<i>Please evacuate to a safe area.</i>

00:16:08.250 --> 00:16:11.380
<i>You are not in any immediate danger.</i>

00:16:12.090 --> 00:16:14.930
<i>The Shibuya Defense Service</i>
<i>has been dispatched.</i>

00:16:15.720 --> 00:16:18.560
Dojima and the others are
doing their best for us.

00:16:18.640 --> 00:16:21.140
I have to hurry!

00:16:24.100 --> 00:16:25.610
What do you think, Marimari?

00:16:27.150 --> 00:16:31.820
Oh, 17 plus 371 years. I get it!

00:16:33.570 --> 00:16:35.280
DAISUKE

00:16:35.990 --> 00:16:37.450
It looks delicious!

00:16:38.120 --> 00:16:41.660
The hotel staff
went out of their way to make it.

00:16:41.830 --> 00:16:43.960
I didn't know we had whipped cream!

00:16:44.170 --> 00:16:46.290
These are canned fruits.

00:16:46.380 --> 00:16:47.540
Really?

00:16:50.590 --> 00:16:52.010
Second one!

00:16:52.880 --> 00:16:54.010
That was quick!

00:16:54.090 --> 00:16:57.220
I've got over 30 hours of practice,
after all!

00:16:57.720 --> 00:16:59.390
Daisuke, you're too close to the center.

00:16:59.470 --> 00:17:00.720
<i>Move to the left!</i>

00:17:00.810 --> 00:17:03.140
<i>-Who cares?</i>
<i>-Obey orders!</i>

00:17:03.230 --> 00:17:05.850
<i>Did you forget what happened</i>
<i>the last time you didn't obey?</i>

00:17:05.940 --> 00:17:07.770
<i>I'm the leader! Obey me!</i>

00:17:07.860 --> 00:17:08.730
<i>What?</i>

00:17:11.980 --> 00:17:15.400
<i>All right, operation complete.</i>
<i>We're heading back, Marin.</i>

00:17:15.860 --> 00:17:17.570
I'll go and get Milo!

00:17:17.660 --> 00:17:18.530
Okay.

00:17:30.500 --> 00:17:32.960
Is this the year 2017?

00:17:33.800 --> 00:17:35.590
It's a ripple in time-space...

00:17:45.520 --> 00:17:46.730
<i>Just as I suspected.</i>

00:17:46.810 --> 00:17:50.020
<i>In a few days, the intersection</i>
<i>between the two times will dissolve.</i>

00:17:50.900 --> 00:17:53.440
<i>Is this due to the conflict</i>
<i>between the Chaotic Orbit</i>

00:17:53.530 --> 00:17:55.440
<i>and the Revisions' quantum brain?</i>

00:18:01.830 --> 00:18:05.450
Just as expected of an AHRV agent.
You've been trained well.

00:18:06.040 --> 00:18:08.710
It won't be possible for me
to kill you in this form.

00:18:08.790 --> 00:18:10.670
Are you with the Revisions?

00:18:12.250 --> 00:18:13.840
This is a good chance.

00:18:14.170 --> 00:18:15.170
Let's talk a bit.

00:18:15.880 --> 00:18:17.300
Why is AHRV interfering

00:18:17.380 --> 00:18:20.640
with the Revisions' plans
of transporting Shibuya?

00:18:21.220 --> 00:18:25.680
Stopping the destruction of humanity is
a pressing issue

00:18:25.770 --> 00:18:28.190
for both the Revisions and AHRV.

00:18:28.270 --> 00:18:31.860
The transport of Shibuya should be in
our best interests considering both our--

00:18:31.940 --> 00:18:33.110
Stop!

00:18:34.030 --> 00:18:35.570
AHRV's predictions of the future

00:18:35.650 --> 00:18:38.820
point to the Revisions'
failure and destruction.

00:18:38.900 --> 00:18:40.490
Making certain of that

00:18:40.700 --> 00:18:43.620
is the means to lead humanity
to the best future!

00:18:43.950 --> 00:18:46.580
The AHRV is as ruthless as ever.

00:18:47.910 --> 00:18:50.040
We are all humans.

00:18:50.710 --> 00:18:51.710
Or are you saying

00:18:52.080 --> 00:18:56.260
that since we manifested symptoms of
the disease and ended up in such a form,

00:18:56.340 --> 00:18:57.970
we should perish?

00:18:58.550 --> 00:19:00.180
"Such a form"?

00:19:00.260 --> 00:19:01.760
How can you say that

00:19:01.840 --> 00:19:04.470
when you have killed
over 100 million AHRV agents?

00:19:06.680 --> 00:19:10.850
The AHRV have acquired humans
capable of using those weapons.

00:19:11.020 --> 00:19:13.480
Since you're sabotaging
the Revisions' plans,

00:19:13.560 --> 00:19:17.400
aren't you the ones taking advantage
of the people of 2017?

00:19:19.200 --> 00:19:23.370
That action is useless
against this remote communication body.

00:19:25.160 --> 00:19:28.450
Using fellow humans as a material
to secure your survival...

00:19:28.580 --> 00:19:31.000
That's certainly not something
a human would do.

00:19:31.170 --> 00:19:32.710
You are all monsters!

00:19:32.790 --> 00:19:36.420
In order to keep your unseemly
and swollen bodies alive,

00:19:36.500 --> 00:19:38.630
<i>you chose to meld with machines.</i>

00:19:39.130 --> 00:19:41.090
<i>When you chose to become monsters,</i>

00:19:41.180 --> 00:19:43.300
<i>the door to your future closed!</i>

00:19:43.390 --> 00:19:45.390
We are not monsters.

00:19:45.640 --> 00:19:48.390
The progression of the disease
caused their intellect to regress,

00:19:48.470 --> 00:19:49.770
but the Civilians are human too!

00:19:52.980 --> 00:19:54.150
Humans?

00:19:54.610 --> 00:19:56.110
Those monsters?

00:19:59.530 --> 00:20:02.030
<i>We've been killing people?</i>

00:20:02.110 --> 00:20:03.200
<i>No way!</i>

00:21:35.040 --> 00:21:36.210
Listen, everyone!

00:21:38.130 --> 00:21:41.170
-Daisuke!
<i>-</i>During that incident with Muta too,

00:21:41.250 --> 00:21:43.670
who knows what would've happened
if I hadn't been there!

00:21:43.760 --> 00:21:46.010
This is a perfect example of what I mean.

00:21:46.090 --> 00:21:50.390
Do you think everything revolves
around you? Don't be ridiculous!

00:21:50.470 --> 00:21:52.600
You're the one being ridiculous!

00:21:52.680 --> 00:21:54.810
Why are you the leader?

00:21:54.930 --> 00:21:57.600
You should just leave this to me!

00:21:57.690 --> 00:21:59.810
-Okay! Just calm down!
-Let go of me!

00:21:59.900 --> 00:22:01.110
I'm the leader!

00:22:01.190 --> 00:22:02.320
There you go again.

00:22:02.530 --> 00:22:03.780
Because I am!

00:22:03.860 --> 00:22:06.740
It doesn't matter
which one of you is the leader!

00:22:07.910 --> 00:22:09.700
Why does this have to happen?

00:22:09.910 --> 00:22:13.700
I thought our friendship returned
to how it was before. Why?

00:22:15.750 --> 00:22:16.960
Marimari.

00:22:23.050 --> 00:22:24.380
What's with you, guys?

00:22:25.340 --> 00:22:27.010
Milo, tell them!

00:22:27.260 --> 00:22:29.470
-He's...
-How foolish!

00:22:29.970 --> 00:22:34.270
Are you all really the String Masters
in the predictions of the future?

00:22:34.770 --> 00:22:37.020
Are you the ones responsible
for the future of humanity?

00:22:37.100 --> 00:22:37.940
What?

00:22:38.520 --> 00:22:39.350
But

00:22:39.650 --> 00:22:42.650
-I--
-It doesn't seem to me like you are

00:22:43.020 --> 00:22:44.320
humans of such worth.

00:22:45.940 --> 00:22:46.820
What?

00:22:49.780 --> 00:22:51.990
Subtitle translation by Emily Noguchi
